I need Prometheus alerting rules for our checkout-api availability SLO: 99.9% of requests over 30 days must be non-5xx. The metric we have is a counter, confirmed via /api/v1/series:

http_server_requests_total{job="checkout-api", namespace="shop", pod="checkout-api-6c9d7-xk2lp", route="/v1/cart", method="POST", code="200"}
http_server_requests_total{job="checkout-api", namespace="shop", pod="checkout-api-6c9d7-xk2lp", route="/v1/cart", method="POST", code="503"}

Note the label is `code`, not `status`. Scrape interval is 30s. The rules get loaded into Mimir's ruler for tenant `shop-prod`. Our current alert is `rate(http_server_requests_total{code=~"5.."}[1m]) > 5` and it pages constantly on blips while missing slow burns. Give me a complete rule group YAML (recording rules for the error ratio plus the alerts) that pages on fast burns and tickets on slow burns.

